WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.563
This session's readings follow new kinds of rides in California.

00:00:04.563 --> 00:00:07.914
First, how ridesharing won over the regulators.

00:00:07.914 --> 00:00:11.194
Then, how robotaxis rose quickly and stumbled.

00:00:11.194 --> 00:00:13.120
Both stories turn on trust.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.551
Lisa Rayle and Onesimo Flores found three reasons.

00:00:16.551 --> 00:00:19.708
Politicians wanted to support local companies.

00:00:19.708 --> 00:00:24.168
Getting a cab was miserable, so riders welcomed something better.

00:00:24.168 --> 00:00:27.600
And ridesharing fell between city and state rules.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.759
Sunil Paul tells the story from the inside.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:36.195
His company, Sidecar, let everyday drivers give rides through a phone app.

00:00:36.195 --> 00:00:38.619
Riders paid a suggested donation.

00:00:38.619 --> 00:00:42.440
It launched in February 2012 and was an instant hit.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.278
Self-driving cars brought new risks.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:51.111
In March 2018, an Uber test car in Tempe, Arizona, killed Elaine Herzberg.

00:00:51.111 --> 00:00:55.920
For five seconds, its software could not decide what she was.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.680
Its safety driver was looking away.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.060
Investigators found a weak safety culture.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:07.693
Uber's self-driving division had no safety manager and no safety plan.

00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:12.040
In October 2017, it cut each car to one safety driver.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:16.309
General Motors bought Cruise in 2016 and grew it fast.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:22.159
In October 2023, a Cruise robotaxi dragged a pedestrian about twenty feet.

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:25.874
Cruise first showed regulators an edited video.

00:01:25.874 --> 00:01:28.800
California then suspended its permit.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.331
Cruise's chief executive, Kyle Vogt, then resigned,

00:01:32.331 --> 00:01:35.446
and the company halted operations nationwide.

00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:38.562
That left Waymo as the clear robotaxi leader.

00:01:38.562 --> 00:01:44.240
New rides grow fast when regulators trust them, and stall when that trust is lost.
